@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy — ThreadCraft Academy</PageTitle>

<article class="legal-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: @LastUpdated.ToString("d MMMM yyyy")</p>

    <p>
        ThreadCraft Academy is a free, no-signup learning tool. There are no user accounts,
        and we do not knowingly collect any information that identifies you personally. This
        page explains, plainly, what data the app does handle.
    </p>

    <h2>Lesson progress</h2>
    <p>
        Which lessons you have passed is stored in a small database on the server so the
        dashboard and checkmarks work. It is not linked to your name, email, or any account —
        there isn't one. Because the app has no login, this progress is shared by everyone
        visiting the same deployment rather than kept separate per visitor.
    </p>

    <h2>The AI coach</h2>
    <p>
        When you ask the "Ask the coach" panel a question, your question, your current code,
        the lesson text, and your recent chat history for that lesson are sent to
        <a href="https://openrouter.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenRouter</a>, a
        third-party API that routes the request to an underlying AI model, in order to
        generate an answer. That data leaves this app and is handled under OpenRouter's own
        privacy policy and that of whichever model answers the request. Don't paste secrets,
        credentials, or anything sensitive into a question or your code — treat it the way
        you'd treat a message to any outside service.
    </p>

    <h2>Your certificate name</h2>
    <p>
        If you use the completion certificate page and type a name for it, that name is saved
        only in your browser's local storage so it's remembered next time you visit. It is
        never sent to the server or to any third party.
    </p>

    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>
        Like any hosted website, the underlying infrastructure (Microsoft Azure) may keep
        standard web server access logs (e.g. IP address, timestamp, requested page) for
        operational and security purposes. We do not use analytics or tracking cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
        This is a small, independently run project. If you have a question about this policy,
        reach out at <a href="mailto:johan.ccs@gmail.com">johan.ccs@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
</article>

@code {
    private static readonly DateOnly LastUpdated = new(2026, 7, 27);
}
